from __future__ import annotations

NAME = "The Beauty of Passing Things"
AMBIENCE = "Gentle Rain"

# A soothing sleep-lecture about the Japanese aesthetics of transience -- mono no aware and wabi-sabi, the loveliness of impermanent, imperfect things.
SECTIONS = [['You are lying down now, and there is nothing left for you to do tonight.', 'Let your body grow heavy, sinking softly into the bed beneath you.', 'The room around you is quiet, and the quiet is kind.', 'Outside the window, the last of the evening light is slowly fading away.', 'You can watch it go, soft and golden, slipping gently toward the dark.', 'There is no need to hold on to the day any longer.', 'Breathe in slowly, and feel the cool air fill you.', 'Breathe out slowly, and feel your shoulders melt down into rest.', 'With each breath, you grow a little softer, a little calmer.', 'Your hands are open, your jaw is loose, your whole body is letting go.', 'Let the day settle around you like dust settling in still air.', 'You are warm, you are safe, and you have all the time in the world to rest.'], ['As you lie here, let your mind grow quiet and slow.', 'Tonight you can think gently about the way that things come and go.', 'Everything you have ever loved has been something passing through.', 'The morning light, a warm afternoon, a song you heard just once.', 'None of these things stayed, and yet each one was lovely.', 'There is a soft truth here, and it is a gentle one, not a sad one.', 'The fact that things do not last is part of what makes them dear.', 'A flower would mean less to you if it bloomed forever.', 'Long ago, poets in Japan felt this very tenderness toward the world.', 'They noticed how the most beautiful things were always quietly slipping away.', 'And instead of fearing it, they let it fill them with a soft, sweet ache.', 'You can feel that same tenderness now, warm and calm, as you drift.'], ['There is a Japanese phrase for this gentle feeling, mono no aware.', 'It means the tender awareness that lovely things are always passing.', 'It is the soft ache you feel when cherry blossoms fall from the branch.', 'The petals are most beautiful in the very moment they let go.', 'They drift down through the air, slow and pink, and settle on the water.', 'No one tries to catch them or hold them back upon the tree.', 'They are simply watched, and loved, and allowed to fall.', 'Think of the last warm evening before the cool of autumn comes.', 'Think of a chord of music, swelling full, then fading into silence.', 'The fading is not a loss, it is the most beautiful part of the sound.', 'The old Japanese poets felt that to notice this was a quiet kind of grace.', 'And you are feeling it now, softly, as your breathing slows and deepens.'], ['There is another gentle idea you can rest in tonight, called wabi-sabi.', 'It is the quiet beauty found in things that are old and worn and humble.', 'A smooth stone with soft green moss spread across its weathered face.', 'A wooden bench gone grey and gentle with many years of rain.', 'A faded cloth, washed a thousand times, soft as a sigh against the skin.', 'A simple clay tea bowl, a little crooked, a little plain, and deeply loved.', 'These things are not perfect, and that is exactly why they are beautiful.', 'Their cracks and their wear are not flaws, but a record of being here.', 'The old Japanese poets felt that nothing needs to be perfect to be precious.', 'Nothing needs to be new, or flawless, or finished, to be worthy of love.', 'And what a great relief that is, to lay down here tonight.', 'You do not have to be perfect either, to deserve this gentle rest.'], ['Let that relief settle over you like a warm and worn old blanket.', 'In Japan there is a beautiful way of mending a bowl that has broken.', 'When a treasured cup cracks, they do not throw it away or hide the break.', 'Instead they mend it carefully, with lacquer mixed with shining gold.', 'They fill each crack with a soft golden seam, slow and patient and kind.', 'And so the very place where it broke becomes the loveliest part of all.', 'The bowl is not worth less for having broken, it is worth more.', 'Its cracks now glow with gold, a quiet map of all it has lived through.', 'This way of mending is called kintsugi, and it is a tender thing.', 'You can think of yourself this way, as the soft night settles in.', 'Every place you have cracked and mended is a thread of gold in you.', 'You do not need to be unbroken to be beautiful, and you may rest.'], ['Now let your thoughts grow slower still, and softer, like falling snow.', 'Tonight you are learning to let things change, and pass, and go.', 'It is the most peaceful thing in the world, to loosen your gentle hold.', 'Like watching petals settle, one by one, upon the surface of still water.', 'You do not reach for them, you only watch them drift and rest.', 'This single quiet moment, just as it is, will never come again.', 'And that is not a sorrow, it is what makes this moment enough.', 'Right now is whole and complete, asking nothing more of you at all.', 'The old poets knew that one passing moment, noticed kindly, is plenty.', 'Breathe in the soft, dim quiet of this room around you.', 'Breathe out, and let this moment be full and finished and enough.', 'There is nowhere else to be, and nothing more that you must do.'], ['And so you let this day be complete, just as it was.', 'It was not a perfect day, and it did not need to be.', 'It was worn and imperfect and humble, and it was enough.', 'Now it is passing, gently, the way that all days pass.', 'You can let it go, like a petal settling softly onto still water.', 'There is nothing left to carry, nothing left to hold, nothing to fix.', 'Your breathing is slow and deep, and your whole body is at rest.', 'Each breath out carries you a little further down into the warm dark.', 'The day is done, and it is good, and it is quietly slipping away.', 'You are soft, and you are mended, and you are enough, exactly as you are.', 'Let yourself drift now, down and down, into the gentle quiet of sleep.', 'Rest now, and sleep, and let this passing moment hold you until morning.']]
